  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have a Udon script that's made to give the player a custom movement system. It uses SetVelocity every FixedUpdated. The problem is Udon changes that velocity before the physics apply it, often setting the velocity to 0 for seemingly no reason. I don't get the point of setting velocity if udon/vrchat is just going to change it again. Immobilize seems to fix this problem, but it locks the players IK which is no good in a lot of situations. I would like the ability to disable the default player movement system without using Immobilize and locking the player's tracking.",
